[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:54.200
"What do you want?"

00:04:57.734 --> 00:04:59.200
Did you guys see this?

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.901
Today, SpaceX launched a crew to
the International Space Station

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:05.968
after the first attempt earlier
this week was cancelled

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:08.767
due to a clogged filter.

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:10.501
Yeah, it's the first time
a space agency

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:13.701
dealt with someone by
calling in the pool guy.

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:15.501
"Trace, you want to take
a look at this?"

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:16.901
"Do I gotta put my shirt on?"

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:18.834
"Hell no."

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:20.234
Yep, a clogged filter.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.901
It's always fun
when a launch delay

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:23.701
can be fixed by someone going...

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.033
Speaking of flight issues,
I heard that

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:31.133
a Spirit Airlines plane
had to make an emergency landing

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:34.534
after a battery in
the overhead bin caught on fire.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:36.267
Spirit was like, "Phew!

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:38.968
Good thing it wasn't
one of our wooden planes."

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:43.033
Wow.

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:45.767
Yeah, the fire was
either caused by a battery

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:47.067
or the pilot was playing with

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:48.934
firecrackers
in the cockpit again.

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:51.267
They got to hire better people.
Listen to this.

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:54.801
Dictionary.com just added
over 300 new words.

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:56.200
That seems like a lot.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.000
And it might explain some other
changes they made, too.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.133
Take a look at this commercial.

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:01.067
-Dictionary.com
is adding 300 new words

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:03.601
to its online database,
such as...

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:07.634
And to make room
for these new additions,

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:10.133
we're eliminating words
that everyone hates, such as...

00:06:22.367 --> 00:06:23.501
-Alright, interesting
Isn't that --

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:25.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:30.701 --> 00:06:32.200
Well, hey, this is fun.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.934
Today is National Read Across
America Day.

00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:36.400
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.434 --> 00:06:40.167
-So, shout-out to everyone

00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:42.067
who's got me on
with subtitles right now.

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:43.968
Hey, you're awesome.

00:06:43.968 --> 00:06:45.968
Yeah, it's National Read Across
America Day,

00:06:45.968 --> 00:06:47.434
so I thought we could
maybe go around

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:49.267
and each share
a book recommendation.

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:50.701
-Yeah.
-I'll go first, okay?

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:52.467
I love "Tomorrow, and Tomorrow,
and Tomorrow"

00:06:52.467 --> 00:06:53.667
by Gabrielle Zevin.

00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:55.767
I highly recommend it.
How about you, Tariq?

00:06:55.767 --> 00:06:58.834
-I gotta go with good old
"Fahrenheit 451."

00:06:58.834 --> 00:07:00.100
-Oh.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.400
-It's a classic dystopian tale
of, you know,

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.801
the dangers of censorship.

00:07:03.801 --> 00:07:06.267
-Oh yeah, that's a good one.
That's a good one. Higgins?

00:07:06.267 --> 00:07:08.634
-You know what?
I like Tolstoy's "War &amp; Peace."

00:07:08.634 --> 00:07:09.701
I know it's long,
but it's worth it.

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:10.801
-"War &amp; Peace."

00:07:10.801 --> 00:07:11.901
I've still got to
check that one out.

00:07:11.901 --> 00:07:14.934
What about you, James?
-Oh, man!

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:17.400
Oh, my favorite book is

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:23.567
"Dr. Schmoyo's Freaky Froyo
Factory" by Todd Nutbush.

00:07:23.567 --> 00:07:25.567
This book has it all, Jimmy --

00:07:25.567 --> 00:07:30.534
humor, romance, thrills,
pure carnal sex...

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:31.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.701 --> 00:07:35.501
...frozen-yogurt recipes,
and heartbreak.

00:07:35.501 --> 00:07:37.868
I couldn't stop crying
while reading it.

00:07:37.868 --> 00:07:41.067
I thought to myself,
"Is someone chopping onions?"

00:07:41.067 --> 00:07:45.534
Sure enough,
my friend Smooth Jeffrey

00:07:45.534 --> 00:07:49.200
was cutting some Vidalia onions
in the same room.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.934
You see, I currently live
with a roommate

00:07:51.934 --> 00:07:56.067
because I lost most of my
savings on NFTs.

00:07:56.067 --> 00:07:58.200
But not those NFTs.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.501
I'm talking...

00:08:00.501 --> 00:08:01.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.934 --> 00:08:03.801
N-- Shut up.

00:08:03.801 --> 00:08:05.534
Nice-fitting top hats.

00:08:05.534 --> 00:08:08.033
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:08:08.033 --> 00:08:09.934
Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:08:13.434 --> 00:08:16.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:16.133 --> 00:08:19.567
-Wow! Wow!

00:08:19.567 --> 00:08:20.934
-What?

00:08:20.934 --> 00:08:23.868
-Smooth Jeffrey said
I look like a leprechaun,

00:08:23.868 --> 00:08:25.767
so I've been working
on my accent.

00:08:25.767 --> 00:08:27.234
Check it out.

00:08:28.834 --> 00:08:34.634
[ Irish accent ] They're always
trying to steal me Irish cereal.

00:08:34.634 --> 00:08:35.934
What do you think?

00:08:35.934 --> 00:08:37.667
Yeah, I probably won't be
getting a call from

00:08:37.667 --> 00:08:40.133
"Mad TV" anytime soon.

00:08:40.133 --> 00:08:41.167
LOL.

00:08:41.167 --> 00:08:43.934
Anyway, happy St. Patrick's Day.

00:08:43.934 --> 00:08:47.200
[ Irish accent ] Don't forget to
read a book today.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:48.767 --> 00:08:54.667
♪♪

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:57.901
-Wow. Is he okay?
-I don't know.

00:08:57.901 --> 00:09:00.968
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.968 --> 00:09:03.567
Guys, I read that
two people in Texas

00:09:03.567 --> 00:09:05.467
