scented-candle-theft ring.

00:09:08.767 --> 00:09:11.434
Yeah, and like
all candle-related crimes,

00:09:11.434 --> 00:09:12.968
they called in John Wick.

00:09:12.968 --> 00:09:16.701
-Oh!
♪♪

00:09:16.701 --> 00:09:19.467
-And, finally, three engineers
broke a world record

00:09:19.467 --> 00:09:24.334
after they made a paper airplane
that flew almost 300 feet.

00:09:24.334 --> 00:09:26.100
Right now,
Spirit Airlines is like,

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.434
"Ah, why didn't
we think of paper?!"

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.734
There is nothing better
than surprising James

00:09:31.734 --> 00:09:34.367
with cue cards during the show,
a live show.

00:09:34.367 --> 00:09:35.901
Thank you for being a
good sport, James.

00:09:35.901 --> 00:09:38.400
What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:39.400
I love this guy.
-I love this guy.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:40.734
-He's unbelievable.

00:09:40.734 --> 00:09:43.033
He's nominated for an
Academy Award for his role in

00:09:43.033 --> 00:09:45.634
"The Whale," which is in
theaters and on demand now.

00:09:45.634 --> 00:09:48.234
Brendan Fraser is here tonight.
-Oh!

00:09:48.234 --> 00:09:50.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:50.868 --> 00:09:52.501
-He's a good man.

00:09:53.767 --> 00:09:57.667
Plus, the new season of
his show, "Next in Fashion,"

00:09:57.667 --> 00:09:59.834
begins streaming
tomorrow on Netflix.

00:09:59.834 --> 00:10:02.300
Fashion expert of
"Queer Eye's" Fab Five,

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:03.334
Tan France is joining us!

00:10:03.334 --> 00:10:06.234
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:06.234 --> 00:10:08.400
-And we got great music
from Lizzy McAlpine,

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.100
ladies and gentlemen.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:11.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
Whoo!

00:10:14.734 --> 00:10:16.400
She's great.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.801
I've been doing a lot of press
for "That's My Jam."

00:10:18.801 --> 00:10:21.000
"That's My Jam" --
season two premieres Tuesday.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.400
I've been doing press.
I've been doing a lot of

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.200
radio interviews and TV
interviews and stuff like that.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.467
And this morning,
I was on one of our pal's,

00:10:28.467 --> 00:10:30.601
"Elvis Duran
and The Morning Show."

00:10:30.601 --> 00:10:31.734
And I went on there --
I love him.

00:10:31.734 --> 00:10:32.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:32.868 --> 00:10:34.968
Hi, Danielle, hi, Gandhi.

00:10:34.968 --> 00:10:36.200
A great crew over there.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:38.167
And they wanted to play a game,
and they said,

00:10:38.167 --> 00:10:40.434
"This is such a dumb game
that we're playing."

00:10:40.434 --> 00:10:42.634
And I go, "I love dumb games.
What is it?"

00:10:42.634 --> 00:10:45.467
And it's called,
"I'm thinking of a pasta."

00:10:45.467 --> 00:10:47.467
[ Laughter ]
That's the name of the game.

00:10:47.467 --> 00:10:49.868
And I go, "Okay."
And, so, the whole idea is,

00:10:49.868 --> 00:10:52.834
Elvis was just thinking of
a pasta, and I had to guess.

00:10:52.834 --> 00:10:54.667
So I thought -- I said,
"I want to take that game.

00:10:54.667 --> 00:10:56.133
I want to play it on
'The Tonight Show,'"

00:10:56.133 --> 00:11:00.133
and he goes, "You'd be out of
your mind to take that game."

00:11:00.133 --> 00:11:01.601
And I am out of my mind,
so here we go.

00:11:01.601 --> 00:11:03.100
We're gonna play the game.

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:05.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Let's do it.

00:11:05.033 --> 00:11:06.300
So, I want to play the game.

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:09.701
Higgins, Tariq, Questlove,
you want to play with me?

00:11:09.701 --> 00:11:11.534
I'm gonna write down a pasta.
-Okay.

00:11:11.534 --> 00:11:14.033
-I'm thinking of a pasta, okay?

00:11:14.033 --> 00:11:17.100
Eh-huh, mm-huh, mm-huh.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.634
[ Laughter ]

00:11:18.634 --> 00:11:22.467
Mm-huh, mm.
-Wait a second.

00:11:22.467 --> 00:11:23.801
-I don't want
to give anything away.

00:11:23.801 --> 00:11:25.167
All right.
Now, here we go.

00:11:25.167 --> 00:11:27.968
I'm thinking of a pasta.
Questlove, what pasta --

00:11:27.968 --> 00:11:31.133
Oh, how 'bout this?
If you guess it right,

00:11:31.133 --> 00:11:33.534
everyone in the audience
gets a pint of

00:11:33.534 --> 00:11:35.334
Tonight Dough Ben &amp; Jerry
ice cream.

00:11:35.334 --> 00:11:37.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:43.033 --> 00:11:45.033
I'm just saying!

00:11:45.033 --> 00:11:46.934
You want to let
these people down?!

00:11:46.934 --> 00:11:49.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
Come on, man.

00:11:49.634 --> 00:11:52.501
Come on, dude!

00:11:52.501 --> 00:11:54.868
All right.
I'm thinking of a pasta.

00:11:54.868 --> 00:11:56.367
-Man, that's a lot of pressure.
-I'm thinking of a pasta.

00:11:56.367 --> 00:11:57.567
Here we go.
-Whoa.

00:11:57.567 --> 00:12:00.100
-All right.
And it falls on me to guess it.

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:02.234
-Well, we have you, Tariq,
and then Higgins, yeah.

00:12:02.234 --> 00:12:03.701
But I'm thinking of a pasta.
-All right.

00:12:03.701 --> 00:12:05.968
I'll go easy.
I'll say rigatoni.

00:12:05.968 --> 00:12:07.467
-Ooh!

00:12:07.467 --> 00:12:09.501
-Not true.
Not good, not good.

00:12:09.501 --> 00:12:10.767
It is not rigatoni.

00:12:10.767 --> 00:12:12.200
Thank you very much.
Come on, focus up.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:13.534
Tariq?
[ Laughter ]

00:12:13.534 --> 00:12:15.567
I am thinking of a pasta.

